    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Long before the town was founded, the land in Carlisle was home to indigenous communities of the Carolina Piedmont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://crdisc.org/history.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Catawba Nation once maintained sophisticated agricultural practices and trade networks throughout the region surrounding Carlisle.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://crdisc.org/history.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Carlisle developed during the nineteenth century as a small rural community shaped by the plantation economy of Union County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
